    "body": "Severity re-judged from the code (issue-worker-high, upstream main ce59ef446):\n\n- **Not P1 for this issue's case.** The entry's rapid to Top + the plunge height inside the stock is convicted by the rapid law (`Warning::RapidInStock`, `blocks_post() == true`); the #1091 stock-top re-read and the #96 prior re-read (`acquit_by_prior`) only acquit a dive the program ahead really cleared, and here the face op only took 0.5 mm. So the program is refused, not posted: by the AGENTS.md table this reads as **P3** (\"a legal program refused\", with a workaround - the air pass at Top), above the P7 it carries. I am not relabelling; the maintainer's call.\n- **A silent case does exist next to it, filed as #2121 (P1):** the rapid law judges rapids *below* the clearance plane only, so a clearance plane set inside the stock rapids through uncut stock and posts with no warning (synthetic repro in that issue).\n\nFix in progress on `issue/1559-2d-entry-below-stock`: the generation reads the material standing over the op's region (stock less the program ahead, the #104 reading) and the 2D ladders (Pocket, 2D Adaptive spiral/trochoidal, Offset, Circular, Contour) start their first descent at the plunge height over it and feed down; a `Carried stock:` note says so. Top on the material posts unchanged.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
